<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">&mdash; the grain and the clock</p>
    <h2 id="t-grain-pace">Why the Grain Gets Finer as the Ascent Gets Faster</h2>
    <p>This chapter has argued that awareness appears at particular grains and is paid for out of the
      record. The <a href="/spiral/#t-pace">pace argument</a> adds the other half of the account: the tick
      of the n-th density goes as 1/n, so each successive turn is traversed faster than the one before.
      Put the two together and a prediction-shaped statement falls out of them.</p>
    <p class="lede">If the interval shortens and the integral still has to be performed, the grain must get
      finer. A faster clock can only be experienced by a system that samples it more densely.</p>
    <p>That is the framework's reading of why ascent feels like intensification rather than extension.
      Nothing is being added to a life; the same integral is being taken over a shorter interval with a
      smaller dx, and the cost of the finer grain is drawn, as always, from the record. The deepening of
      experience and the thinning of memory are the same transaction seen from two sides.
      <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p>There is a floor, and it is not rhetorical. Landauer's principle fixes the minimum energy to erase
      one bit at k<sub>B</sub>T&thinsp;ln&thinsp;2 &mdash; about 2.9 &times; 10<sup>&minus;21</sup> J at
      300 K, measured in 2012 &mdash; so a grain cannot be refined without limit at finite temperature and
      finite energy. The ascent does not get infinitely fine; it gets as fine as the thermodynamics will
      sell. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p class="muted">Against ourselves: &ldquo;the integral is taken over a shorter interval&rdquo; assumes
      that the quantity of experience per density is conserved, and nothing here establishes that. It is the
      assumption that makes the paragraph work, and it is named rather than hidden.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<!-- expand:dx:end -->

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="lede">Nothing wakes for free. Every grain fine enough to know itself is bought out of the
      record of what it was &mdash; which is why becoming more present and remembering more faithfully have
      always felt like opposite labours.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Next: <a href="/gravity/">gravity as the curvature of the geometry</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
